# Intent: Four more rule sets for the grid game engine, as pure cores with host tests: Hangman (a word table, 26 keys in 3 rows, seven misses), the 2048-style slider (4 by 4, seeded tiles, merge once per slide, won at 2048), Snake (10 by 8 board, steer by direction, speeds up with each food, dies on a wall or itself) and Mine Finder (8 by 8, 10 mines, the first reveal is never a mine, flood fill, flags). Nothing draws or starts them yet: the device layer, and the inputs Snake and the slider need (swipe up and down), follow. A game never moves the head.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: nothing to check on the unit yet (the cores are not used by any device file); host/tests/firmware/grid_games2_test.c is the check.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none yet (headers only). Planned per running game, in PSRAM: Hangman 50 bytes, slider 30, Snake about 220, Mines 70; nothing while no game runs.

